+# Test Suite for orders_enrichment DAG
+
+## Overview
+This pytest suite validates the financial data transformation logic of the `orders_enrichment` DAG without relying on Airflow decorators or a running scheduler.
+
+**Total Tests:** 32 (all passing)
+
+## Test Coverage
+
+### 1. Deduplication (`TestDedupeOrders` - 5 tests)
+- Single order per ID: no deduplication needed
+- Multiple versions: keeps latest by `updated_at` timestamp
+- Output is sorted by order_id
+- Complex scenario: mixed single/multi versions
+- Empty input handling
+
+**Finance Impact:** Prevents double-counting when orders are exported multiple times.
+
+### 2. FX Conversion (`TestConvertToUSD` - 9 tests)
+- USD to USD (rate=1)
+- EUR to USD with realistic rates
+- GBP to USD with realistic rates
+- HALF_UP rounding (e.g., 51.435 → 51.44)
+- Missing FX rate raises ValueError with order details
+- Multiple orders with one missing rate
+- All fields preserved in output
+- Zero amount handling
+- Large amounts (7-8 digits) converted accurately
+
+**Finance Impact:** Ensures correct monetary conversion with proper rounding (matches accounting standards).
+
+### 3. Validation (`TestValidateTotals` - 8 tests)
+- Valid orders pass through
+- Rejects orders with missing customer_id (empty string)
+- Rejects orders with None customer_id
+- Rejects orders with negative amount_usd
+- Rejects multiple bad orders in one batch
+- Accepts zero amounts (valid for adjustments)
+- Accepts whitespace customer_id (string is truthy)
+- Empty input handling
+
+**Finance Impact:** Prevents invalid records from entering the output file.
+
+### 4. Data Loading (`TestExtractOrders` & `TestLoadFXRates` - 4 tests)
+- Extract: filters orders by order_date
+- Extract: returns empty list for no match
+- FX Rates: loads rates for the given date
+- FX Rates: always includes USD with rate=1
+
+**Finance Impact:** Ensures data is correctly read from source files with proper date filtering.
+
+### 5. End-to-End Integration (`TestEndToEndWithSampleData` - 3 tests)
+- Full pipeline on 2026-03-02 sample data
+- Output file has correct columns: order_id, customer_id, currency, amount, amount_usd
+- File is only written after validation passes (if validation fails, no file)
+
+**Finance Impact:** Validates the complete data transformation flow on realistic sample data.
+
+### 6. Failure Scenarios (`TestIntegrationWithFailures` - 3 tests)
+- Missing FX rate stops the pipeline (raises ValueError)
+- Validation failure prevents file write (no output created)
+- Timestamp string comparison works correctly for deduplication
+
+**Finance Impact:** Ensures pipeline fails safely on data issues rather than producing invalid output.
+
+## Running the Tests
+
+```bash
+pytest tests/
+pytest tests/ -v                    # Verbose output
+pytest tests/ -k "test_convert"     # Run specific tests
+pytest tests/ --tb=short            # Short traceback on failures
+```
+
+## Test Data
+- Sample orders: `data/orders.csv` (2026-03-01, 2026-03-02)
+- Sample FX rates: `data/fx_rates.csv` (2026-03-01, 2026-03-02)
+- Output: `output/orders_enriched/` (created by integration tests)
+
+## Implementation Notes
+- All transformation functions are extracted to `tests/helpers.py` to avoid Airflow decorator complexity
+- Tests use `pytest` fixtures and temporary directories for isolation
+- Financial rounding uses `Decimal` with `ROUND_HALF_UP` to match accounting standards
+- No DAG code was modified; helpers.py contains pure Python copies of transformation logic
